WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:16.699
Good morning John. I'm in a donut. Omnomnomnom.

00:00:16.699 --> 00:00:38.930
I'm at Google headquarters. I've had a bit
of a whirlwind week; it's been a little bit

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.989
insane, but now, I'm in San Francisco, and
this place is cool. They have little bikes

00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:45.489
you can borrow. Take 'em around. We started
off in Seattle, where I saw what I thought

00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:48.870
was the largest window ever. And then I went
to Los Angeles and saw a bunch of convention

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:52.219
centers where the windows were much larger
than that one in Seattle. And now I'm at at

00:00:52.219 --> 00:00:55.829
Google, which is pretty amazing fairyland
of a place, to be honest.

00:00:55.829 --> 00:01:00.730
And now they gave me an o-, I officaly have
an office at Google. Look at me, look at it.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:05.880
I officially, actually I just walked into
this room. I, I opened the door and I walked

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:12.130
in. 'Cause there's a plug, and there's a desk
and I, I needed to edit my video. Ahhh! Careful,

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:15.119
camera. Don't fall over, you're expensive.

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:19.600
It's weird here. You know how recently, people
found out that Google had been driving a car

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.030
that was driving itself, and the driver wasn't
driving, and it was driving all around California,

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:26.770
and nobody knew about it? People who work
on things like that, they call them product

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:31.790
development. Product developers. It's kinda
like saying, uh, my job is that I, uh, I'm

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:37.020
a stuff maker. I make stuff. That almost freaks
me out, like sometimes, you know how recently

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.870
scientists said they could, uh, possibly make
a human-chipanzee hybrid? And that's kinda

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:44.329
like an interesting and cool idea, but of
course you never want to do that, it's really

00:01:44.329 --> 00:01:48.620
immoral, but it's, scientifically, it's very
fascinating, very fascinating idea. I feel

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:53.399
like 70 floors below me right now, there is
a humanzee. And they're... putting him through

00:01:53.399 --> 00:01:56.630
grade school, and you know, maybe they'll
make him a humanzee girlfriend at some point.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:59.689
Honestly, it's just amazing to see all the
people who come together and make the things

00:01:59.689 --> 00:02:03.409
that make our lives better. Ahh, they seem
very happy, like very nice people. The food

00:02:03.409 --> 00:02:07.759
is delicious. Almost certain that they're
not making any kind of chimeras. It's really,

00:02:07.759 --> 00:02:08.759
it's a good place.

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:13.820
Ahh, and if were to actually curious why I
was in Los Angeles-- Why does my finger smell

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.400
like chocolate? Why am I not editing this
out of the video?

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.060
Working on Vidcon, I was working on Vidcon
in Los Angeles. And now I'm here at Google

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:24.880
to attend the first Google-only stop of the
Digitour. Which I'm very exited about, and

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:28.840
it may be coming to a place near you. Just
Google it, and there's a good chance it's

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:29.840
gonna be at a city near you. Thank you to
Alex Day for the song that's been playing

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.410
in the background of this video. It's called
Hearts, and it's on his album Parrot Stories.

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:36.510
John, I hope that you aren't too jealous that
I am the first vlogbrother that got to go

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:51.379
to Mountain View campus of Google. I will
see you, on a day that is Monday.

